Z||000000||Kage86GT4SP||07-06-99||12:38 AM||||yeah... I found out the hard way.<p>Now I don't get an idle below 1800 rpm.  The engine doesn't stall, its just that the idle won't drop below 1800.  Ocassionally, I get a 1800-1500 rythmic swing... but then it goes away and back to a steady 1800.<p>The only code I get is 21 (Throttle Position Sensor)<p>When the engine is cold, I can move the TPS manually, and the engine will dramatically change in speed.  When the engine gets to operating temp, moving the TPS makes no difference.<p>With the exception of the idle, the engine runs fine.  Its a stone-stock 2.8, and the car had not been driven for around 2 years.<p>What should I be looking for?  <p>Any ideas or emails would be helpful, because I don't think I can get this thing smogged until I get this fixed.<p>Thanks!  <p>K.<p>(kage@pacifier.com)
Z||000001||theogre||07-06-99||03:33 PM||||was the motor hot when you washed it? if it was you likely cracked some part of the exhaust.
